{"id":"3F","title":"Hatred and Malice","part":{"n":3,"title":"Relationship to Other Persons"},"url":"/law/03-relationship-to-other-persons/3f","entries":[{"id":"3F.1","text":"Thou shall not hate your brethren in your heart.","refs":[{"book":"Leviticus","chapter":19,"verses":"17"},{"book":"Colossians","chapter":3,"verses":"8"},{"book":"1 John","chapter":3,"verses":"15"}],"citation":"Lev. 19:17; Col. 3:8; 1 John 3:15."},{"id":"3F.2","text":"Wrath is a work of the flesh.","refs":[{"book":"Galatians","chapter":5,"verses":"20"}],"citation":"Gal. 5:20."},{"id":"3F.3","text":"It is wicked to have hatred cloaked by deceit.","refs":[{"book":"Proverbs","chapter":10,"verses":"18"},{"book":"Proverbs","chapter":26,"verses":"24-26"}],"citation":"Prov. 10:18; Prov. 26:24-26."},{"id":"3F.4","text":"Hatred stirs up strife","refs":[{"book":"Proverbs","chapter":10,"verses":"12"},{"book":"Proverbs","chapter":15,"verses":"18"}],"citation":"Prov. 10:12; Prov. 15:18."},{"id":"3F.5","text":"Hatred is inconsistent with the ways of God.","refs":[{"book":"1 John","chapter":2,"verses":"9,11"},{"book":"1 John","chapter":4,"verses":"20"}],"citation":"1 John 2:9, 11; 1 John 4:20."},{"id":"3F.6","text":"Blessed are you, when men shall hate you, and ostracized you, insult you, and spurn your name as evil, for the sake of Christ.","refs":[{"book":"Luke","chapter":6,"verses":"22"}],"citation":"Luke 6:22."},{"id":"3F.7","text":"Let none of you think evil in your heart against your neighbor.","refs":[{"book":"Zechariah","chapter":8,"verses":"17"}],"citation":"Zech. 8:17."},{"id":"3F.8","text":"Whosoever is angry with his brother without cause shall be in danger of judgment.","refs":[{"book":"Matthew","chapter":5,"verses":"22"}],"citation":"Matt. 5:22."},{"id":"3F.9","text":"Show no malice nor desire ill will towards your brethren.","refs":[{"book":"Job","chapter":31,"verses":"29-30"},{"book":"Psalms","chapter":35,"verses":"12-14"},{"book":"1 Corinthians","chapter":14,"verses":"20"},{"book":"Colossians","chapter":3,"verses":"8"}],"citation":"Job. 31:29-30; Psa. 35:12-14; 1 Cor. 14:20; Col. 3:8."},{"id":"3F.10","text":"Christian growth requires that you set aside all malice and guile.","refs":[{"book":"1 Peter","chapter":2,"verses":"1"}],"citation":"1 Pet 2: 1."},{"id":"3F.11","text":"Malice works as leaven and is incompatible with sincerity and truth.","refs":[{"book":"1 Corinthians","chapter":5,"verses":"8"}],"citation":"1 Cor. 5:8."},{"id":"3F.12","text":"There is a time to hate.","refs":[{"book":"Ecclesiastes","chapter":3,"verses":"8"}],"citation":"Eccl. 3:8."},{"id":"3F.13","text":"Christian liberty is not to be made a cloak for maliciousness.","refs":[{"book":"1 Peter","chapter":2,"verses":"16"}],"citation":"1 Pet 2:16."},{"id":"3F.14","text":"We should hate those that hate God.","refs":[{"book":"Psalms","chapter":139,"verses":"21-22"}],"citation":"Psa. 139:21-22."},{"id":"3F.15","text":"A servant of God is to be gentle to all men.","refs":[{"book":"1 Thessalonians","chapter":2,"verses":"7"},{"book":"2 Timothy","chapter":2,"verses":"24"},{"book":"Titus","chapter":3,"verses":"2"},{"book":"James","chapter":3,"verses":"17"}],"citation":"1 Thes. 2:7; 2 Tim. 2:24; Titus 3:2; James 3:17."}]}